                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First impressions based on 30 mins play time is that the game has promise. The setting is on a space ship returning to Earth and the object is to kill the creatures that escaped during transit. \n\nYou play in a very dark enviroment with some light showing on computer screens and other panels around you. This light helps but is not enough to light up the dark room you're in. This is where you need to rely on your hand scanner (place your two hands together in a clap motion to activate that) and the torches on each pistol you carry.\n\nYou progress through to the next room using locomotion once you've cleared the room you are in first. You will need to use your scanner as some of the creatures are small and hard to spot. Once you know where they are, you move your hands apart and automatically equip pistols in both hands. Each pistol has a torch that light up the room in front of you helping you to shoot the creatures in your line of sight. Putting both weapons together (one in front of the other) they combine into a sort of lazer/plasma rifle. Moving your hands back from that position returns your pistols.\n\nI didn't notice a health bar while in game yet I knew I was being hit by something as small slatters of blood was visibly hitting the screen edges. Will you eventually die at some point, I have yet to find out. I also got the impression that you go from room to room set in a large square. No corridors were available to go through into another level which I assume will come as you level up or later.\n\nPros:\n\nSmall download and is quick to load up.\nGood graphics and smooth simplistic game play.\nMinimal use of controller buttons (fire buttons seem to be the main ones used).\nPlayed in Standing mode on VR\n\nCons:\n\nNo ability to exit the game or return to the starting room once you are playing a level.\nCould get repetative.\nNo score or health bar!\n\nAs I said at the start, this game shows promise. A good effort by the developer :) \n\nRating: 7/10",
